libc++ (LLVM 18) <functional>: std::function<int(int)> holding a lambda
returned a nondeterministic value.  Fixed: the virtual call of
__func::operator() (cpp11_virtual_override_with_rvalue_reference_parameter),
and the __tuple_impl constructor bodies dropped because overload resolution
for __compressed_pair_elem's constructor also offered the specialization
instantiated for the other __alloc_func constructor (tuple<int &&>) for a
tuple<> argument, whose conversion trial instantiated tuple<int &&>'s
constructor template with tuple<> ([temp.over]/1,
cpp11_deduction_fails_for_mismatched_template_argument_count).  clang++ 18
-stdlib=libc++ accepts this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
